  "aboutParagraphs": [
    "Agnes Moffitt is Houston's flat, tree-lined 21-hole course — numerous trees and a friendly layout at 5,911 feet and par 63 from the short tees. Andi Lehmann's 1993 design works on two levels: the red posts make a fun casual round, the white posts add distance and difficulty.",
    "Free to play with concrete tees and Dynamic Veteran baskets, it's very cart friendly with restrooms on site. The trees are the whole game here — every fairway has a line, and every line has a tree waiting for the careless.",
    "A classic Houston park course that rewards a calm, accurate round."
  ],
